thetical plateau is not an added premise of the full-support theorem. Fixed finite-step smooth-terminal data only; constants may depend on these data. This leaf includes heat-kernel construction and Gaussian convolution estimates. No uniform-in-approximation tail assertion or minimizer hypothesis is made.","citation_ids":["support_tails_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"id":"support.step_tails","kind":"claim","label":"Finite-step density transform and differentiated tails","locator":"signs.tex:17–167; tail:class","source_id":"support_tex_signs","statement":"Fix 0=t0<...<tN=1, 0<c1<=...<=cN<=M, gamma=ci on each step, terminal Phi(1,x)=M^(-1)log(2cosh(Mx)), and the associated diffusion from 0. On a step of height c, set l=cPhi, r=l_x, v=r_x, w=r_xx, z=r_xxx and factor the positive density f=e^l g. Then g evolves by forward heat, g_+=g_- exp(-delta Phi) at upward jumps, and s=-partial_x log g is odd. At positive times away from 0, the source proves differentiated exponential backward tails and Gaussian-times-exponential forward tails, so s=x/t-beta(t)+exponentially decaying error.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/support.step_tails","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/support.backward_shapes","id":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22support.backward_shapes%22%2C%22support.step_tails%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22support.backward_shapes%22%2C%22support.step_tails%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/support.step_tails"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","fr